WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.450
The third and final movie in the To All The
Boys trilogy is finally here and it's filled

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:09.610
with incredible details from cheeky Kitty
call-backs and sweet treat easter eggs to

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:10.719
secret cameos.

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:14.809
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan, and
today I'm revealing all the hidden adorable

00:00:14.809 --> 00:00:17.210
references you missed in Always and Forever.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.779
Of course, spoilers ahead if you haven't seen
it yet.

00:00:19.779 --> 00:00:24.190
The movie kicks off with Lara Jean writing
to Peter from Seoul in a café that looks

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.910
like it's ripped straight from the pages of
a comic book.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:31.150
The amazing thing is that this isn't a set
but a real-life coffee shop in Seoul that's

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:35.280
been deliberately painted all white with black
outlines to create the illusion that you're

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.170
in a 2D cartoon.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:41.020
Named after its street number, the café is
an incredibly popular location, especially

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.710
for posting on Instagram.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:47.110
And the way it's used in the movie, along
with some of the film's comic-book-style transitions,

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:51.460
really reminded me of A-Ha's video for Take
On Me, which feels especially fitting given

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:53.820
LJ's love of 80s pop culture.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:58.469
And another cute detail in the Korean café
scene is that the postcard that Lara Jean

00:00:58.469 --> 00:01:01.140
writes to Peter has the words Seoulmates on
the front,

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:05.590
pointing to the fact that even though they
are already thousands of miles apart, LJ and

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:07.600
PK are still destined to be together.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.290
"I love you, Peter.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:10.290
Always and forever."

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:11.700
"Like a lingering fart.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.780
Or nay, a bruise that never heals."

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:18.229
During Lara Jean's make-believe montage of
her future life with Peter after she imagines

00:01:18.229 --> 00:01:23.150
getting into Stanford, she sees herself signing
a book she's written called "Whoa, Whoa, Whoa".

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.860
This is a funny nod to Peter's catchphrase
from the first movie.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:26.869
"Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:01:26.869 --> 00:01:28.210
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:29.220
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:30.220
Whoa, whoa.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:31.220
Hey, hey, hey.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:32.220
Whoa, whoa, whoa..."

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:35.520
Although fans didn't get any "whoa, whoa,
whoas" in the second film, this moment in

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.680
the new movie is a little tribute to the huge
sensation and meme those words from Peter

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.780
became after the success of the first film.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:47.500
Another image we see in LJ's imagined future
is her and Peter painting their home together.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:52.229
As LJ watches on, Peter paints a big blue
heart with their initials in the middle, a

00:01:52.229 --> 00:01:56.810
moment which reminded me of how LJ painted
a blue heart on a lantern after their first

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:58.850
real date in the second movie.

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:03.479
And those blue hearts in both films fit perfectly
with the trilogy's colour palette which relies

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:06.481
heavily on cyans,
as well as magentas and yellows as we can

00:02:06.481 --> 00:02:11.620
see from the character's clothes, as well
as the films' sets, props, and cinematography.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:15.940
And those signature colours, magenta, cyan
and yellow, are the same ones that the filmmakers

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:20.750
used to light the Empire State Building for
the New York rooftop party scene.

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:25.000
When Peter surprises the Coveys after they
get back from Korea, Kitty compliments him

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.300
on his "Welcome Home" sign.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:29.970
"Your spatial planning could use work, but
I appreciate the glitter."

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:34.230
Which is a nice nod to this moment in the
second movie where Kitty used glitter for

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:38.420
the Valentine's card she secretly sent to
Mrs Rothschild on behalf of her dad.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.280
"Dad's not a glitter type of guy."

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:44.060
"Nor were you a Peter Kavinsky kinda girl
till I sprinkled some glitter on it."

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:46.660
Genevieve complimenting Lara Jean's footwear
in "Always and Forever"..

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:47.660
"Oh, my God, cute shoes.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:48.660
I like those."

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:53.400
..is a call-back to how Gen commented sarcastically
on LJ's boots in the first movie

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.400
"Cute boots.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.600
Thank you so much for your service."

00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:00.820
Notice how Lara Jean and Genevieve's position
in the hallway has been switched around this

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:03.870
time making this moment a mirror of the original
scene

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:07.720
and showing how they are both back to being
friends now rather than the antagonists they

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.090
were at the start of the first film.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:14.350
Author Jenny Han's cameo in each of the movies
has become a tradition, and in Always and

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:18.400
Forever she makes a brief appearance in the
flashback scene of LJ and PK's meet-cute.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:23.900
Han plays Principal Cho who calls Lara Jean
on stage to receive an attendance award.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:27.920
According to the filmmakers, her appearances
– as a middle school principal in the first

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:31.500
and third movies, and as Adler High's vice
principal in the second movie

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.950
– give her character a mini career arc across
the trilogy.

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:40.070
By the way, the same crying girl that Jenny
Han was comforting on Valentine's Day in P.S.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:44.310
I Still Love You, has a much happier moment
in Always and Forever when she's the recipient

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:45.370
of a musical promposal.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:48.090
"Molly Marshall, will you go to prom with
me?"

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:49.350
"Yes, of course.

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:50.350
Yes!"

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:54.780
When LJ organises a "perfect" date with Peter,
she takes some inspiration from the classic

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:59.560
Coen Brothers' crime-comedy The Big Lebowski
and plans an evening at a local bowling alley,

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:03.730
where she sets their table with some tasty
treats for them to eat, including the same

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:09.090
kind of fruit turnovers she made for Peter
as a Valentine's Day gift in the second movie.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:13.320
When Lara Jean is planning the perfect date,
she compiles a list of some of Peter's favourite

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:14.740
films for ideas.

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:18.970
It's mostly made up of action movies like
"Fast and Furious" but an interesting one

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:23.380
is "X-Men: Apocalypse", because that's the
film in which Lana Condor made her acting

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:25.320
debut as the mutant Jubilee.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.210
"This is Scott.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:28.720
He's new here too."

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:32.850
And this might be a little stretch, but the
movie "This Is The End" has been crossed out,

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:37.090
perhaps foreshadowing that although "Always
and Forever" is the final movie in the series,

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:41.820
this won't be the end of LJ and PK's story
as they choose to stay together at university

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:43.810
despite the many miles between them.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:47.720
Oh, and Doctor Sleep appears on the list as
the director of the second and third To All

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:52.590
The Boys films, Michael Fimognari, was the
cinematographer on that movie.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:56.500
Butterflies keep cropping in the new film,
from the poster in Lara Jean's English classroom,

00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:01.160
to various knick-knacks in her bedroom, to
the ones on lockers at school.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:06.080
Culturally, butterflies are often symbols
of transformation, freedom, and new beginnings,

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:11.080
all themes that are crucial in the final film
as Lara Jean is on the verge of a new life,

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:15.090
making big decisions that will take her from
her final days as a school girl to her new

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:17.480
future as a university student.

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:21.870
Which is why we also see a large butterfly
poster, as well as a 'follow your heart' poster,

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:26.611
in Margot's college room in Scotland, as she's
already making her own life for herself, and

00:05:26.611 --> 00:05:29.330
encourages LJ to do the same.

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:33.960
As well as butterflies pointing to the theme
of change in LJ's life, the film is full of

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:38.500
posters that foreshadow her decision to choose
New York University over Berkeley.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:43.180
Even before LJ knows that she's been accepted
to NYU, at school there are New York posters

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:45.980
with the Statue of Liberty all around Peter.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:50.550
And as they all hand in their permission slips
for the east-coast trip, we see posters including

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:55.090
one with the words 'How Far Will You Go?',
a drawing of a woman with a question mark

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:59.460
over her signalling how LJ will question her
decision about university,

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:03.950
and a poster of another woman with the words
'Own Your Story', which feels especially fitting

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:08.660
because as LJ's dad tells her later:
"Listen Lara Jean, you got to stay true to

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:11.400
yourself;
you can't save this relationship by not growing."

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:15.901
Likewise, when LJ's struggling to decide whether
she should follow her desire to go to NYU,

00:06:15.901 --> 00:06:20.620
and asks Gen whether she should go,
she's standing next to posters that feature

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:25.330
the Statue of Liberty, the words 'Do what
you love', and 'You are stronger than you

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:26.330
think'!

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:30.640
The fabric box that Lara Jean fills with memories
of their relationship and gives to Peter is

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:34.990
actually the same box that held LJ's letters
to all the boys she'd loved before,

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:39.580
which gives it extra emotional value because
it was instrumental in how LJ and Peter's

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:41.830
relationship began.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:46.340
After Lara Jean accidentally texts Peter that
she got into Stanford, to celebrate he turns

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:49.880
up outside her house recreating the iconic
scene from "Say Anything",

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:53.980
the 80s rom com where the male lead holds
up a boombox to prove his love.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:56.760
"There's this great scene with John Cusack,
and he sits underneath the window.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:57.760
And he holds up a boombox..

00:06:57.760 --> 00:06:58.760
Okay!"

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:02.550
Lara Jean's love of classic 80s movies has
been a hallmark of her story in this trilogy,

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:06.650
from her recreating the opening scene of "Adventures
in Babysitting" at the beginning of P.S.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:09.740
I Still Love You,
to the rule she made in the first movie that

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:14.450
Peter could put his hand in her back pocket,
an idea taken from the opening scene of "Sixteen

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.450
Candles".

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:18.080
And she acknowledges this in her closing monologue
of this movie.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:19.310
"My whole life..

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:22.800
I've wanted the kind of love you see in the
movies.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:27.200
Boombox over the head, hand in the back pocket
of your jeans kind of love."

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:31.300
At the beginning of the movie, we see Lara
Jean reading Pride and Prejudice, and the

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:35.610
film also draws attention to her packing the
classic novel for her trip to New York.

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:40.300
As a romantic comedy of manners, it's clear
why Pride and Prejudice would appeal to LJ,

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:44.420
but I think the book is also alluding to how
she and Peter both grow and mature in their

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:47.930
relationship throughout the final film, and
trilogy as a whole,

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:52.180
similar to how the main protagonists in Jane
Austen's novel work to overcome their flaws

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:54.410
to ultimately achieve a happy romantic union.

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:55.410
"Do you dance, Mr Darcy?"

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:56.970
"Not if I can help it."

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:59.200
"Do you dance, Mr. Kavinsky?"

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:00.200
"Mm.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.200
Not if I can help it."

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:05.770
And the repeated Pride and Prejudice references
may also be a little nod to the third book

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:09.770
in Jenny Han's trilogy where LJ creates a
mood board featuring the Pride &amp; Prejudice

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:11.580
movie for her dad and Trina's wedding.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:15.070
Oh, and let's not forget that LJ's sister
Kitty, aka Katherine..

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:16.070
"I'm Katherine.

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:18.680
That was weird, that's not my name.

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:19.680
Kitty.

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:21.389
Well, Katherine's kind of my name, but people
don't call me that.

00:08:21.389 --> 00:08:22.389
Call me Kitty.

00:08:22.389 --> 00:08:23.389
You can call me whatever."

00:08:23.389 --> 00:08:27.800
shares her name with one of the characters
in Jane Austen's famous novel.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:31.870
Lara Jean's love of Harry Potter in the original
books was touched upon in the second movie

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:36.510
in a flashback scene where she's reading The
Prisoner of Azkaban together with John Ambrose,

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:40.729
and Harry Potter comes up again in the third
film when it turns out that LJ's sister Kitty

00:08:40.729 --> 00:08:45.310
is also a huge Potter-head, and she's outraged
to discover her Korean boyfriend [Dae] hates

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:46.310
it.

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:49.800
He said, and I quote, "that it's so dumb."

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.620
How am I supposed to be in a relationship
with someone who thinks the greatest literary

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:55.120
achievement of our time is dumb?

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:58.520
And if you want to discover all the easter
eggs and incredible details you missed in

00:08:58.520 --> 00:08:59.520
P.S.

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:03.380
I Still Love You as well, tap here to watch
that video or follow the link in the video

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:04.380
description.

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:06.870
So, what did you think of Always and Forever?

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:10.480
Did you like the ending and were there any
other interesting details you noticed?

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:12.950
Leave your thoughts in the comments below!

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:16.250
And if you enjoyed this video, then I really
appreciate a thumbs-up.

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:20.430
Tap left to watch my next Netflix video or
tap right for something else you're sure to

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:21.430
like.

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:23.080
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:23.980
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

